{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Tightened the CI monitor: it was reporting expected noise, which is how a real signal gets missed overnight\n\nFour consecutive monitor events were draining pre-fix Gerrit runs -- every one with headSha\n6125c5345f01, i.e. the commit before the 9a17 fix merged. Each was correctly benign, and I verified\neach individually with 'git merge-base --is-ancestor 668523feffde <headSha>' rather than assuming.\n\nBut four identical 'expected' notifications in a row is precisely how a genuine recurrence gets\nskimmed past at 3am. So I moved the ancestor test INTO the monitor rather than doing it by hand each\ntime. It now reports:\n - a FAILING run ONLY when its head CONTAINS 668523feffde -- labelled 'FAILED(post-fix, ACTIONABLE)'\n - every branch-head (Test Suite) result on main, pass or fail\nand is silent otherwise. Pre-fix runs are suppressed at source.\n\nThis is the same principle as the two signal-quality tickets filed tonight (f850 windows sweep, 337e\nbrowser tier): a warning that is always present carries no information, and worse, it trains the\nreader to ignore the channel it arrives on. Fixing my own monitor rather than continuing to\nhand-filter is the consistent move.\n\nNote I checked my own work here too -- the FIRST monitor I wrote was silently broken: its Python read\nos.environ['SEEN'] while the shell only set a local variable, never exported, so it would have\nemitted nothing at all while appearing armed. A blind watch is worse than no watch, because it\nmanufactures false confidence. Caught before relying on it; worth remembering that an armed monitor\nshould be proven to emit at least once before it is trusted.\n\nMeanwhile dispatched an agent on 477b (toolchain fast-path race) to use the hold productively --\nsmall, fully specified, branched from current main so it carries both fixes. Deliberately NOT\ndispatching 3276 / 9ea3 / bff5: their changes would only queue behind the scanner blocker, and\nflooding a degraded CI queue with five more runs helps nobody. 337e and f850 await a support-target\ndecision rather than code, so there is nothing to implement on them yet."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788502932160482001,"uuid":"d242e021-7b82-49fb-ad73-35f03ba8ce13"}